      "writtenOn": "2020-01-07T01:11:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "if the requirement is just min 1000 samples at once, then we can actually do better that packing the max number of LCM(1000*TSB, 32) blocks into a packet, since we don\u0027t care about the number of blocks per packet at all (as long as it\u0027s more than 1).\nwhat we need is the biggest number that divides by 4 and TSB, which is not bigger that 2032. \n(we also need to check that this number is at least 1000*TSB/8 \u003d 125*TSB. but we are guaranteed to find this number in the top TSB*4, and ((2032 - TSB*4) / TSB) * TSB \u003d (2032 / TSB) * TSB - 4 * TSB \u003e 2032 - 5*TSB \u003e 125*TSB, for TSB \u003c\u003d 15; and for 16, 2032 is divisable by both 4 and 16, so again 2032 \u003e 2000, so always holds for TSB in 1..16 range, no need to check)\n\nexample for TSB\u003d1. what we get with the current calculation is:\nsample_size \u003d GCD(125*1,4) \u003d 512\nsample_size \u003d (2032/512) * 512 \u003d 3*512 \u003d 1536\nto get to TRNG_SAMPLE_COUNT of 1000000, we need (1000000+1535)/1536 \u003d 652 calls.\n\nif we went with (2032 / TSB) * TSB, we\u0027d get full 2032 samples out from every request, so would do only (1000000+2031)/2032 \u003d 493 calls. This way, no need to waste time on processing 159 extra requests. More time exercising TRNG, less time in communication stack.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 75,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 75,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "7f58c9afe36874fd0942637305a533c994c1b5ec",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
